00:05:35.092 --> 00:05:35.925
(shouting)

00:05:35.925 --> 00:05:36.758
- Calm down man, calm down.

00:05:36.758 --> 00:05:37.591
(shouting)

00:05:37.591 --> 00:05:38.424
- Get him out already.

00:05:38.424 --> 00:05:39.371
- I'm trying.

00:05:39.371 --> 00:05:40.204
- Come on.

00:05:40.204 --> 00:05:42.454
(crashing)

00:05:44.364 --> 00:05:46.660
(panting)

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:47.840
- We still have no idea why he was

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:49.000
in the coma to begin with.

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:51.630
- Or why he woke up. I
wonder if it is hormonal.

00:05:51.630 --> 00:05:54.310
Acute adrenal insufficiency
could cause a temporary coma.

00:05:54.310 --> 00:05:58.090
- It can, and also a thyroid
storm can cause a coma.

00:05:58.090 --> 00:06:00.350
Although a thyroid storm
would probably come

00:06:00.350 --> 00:06:03.560
with a rapid heart rate,
also not weight gain.

00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:05.216
If you have a hyperactive thyroid,

00:06:05.216 --> 00:06:07.650
although if you have
an underactive thyroid

00:06:07.650 --> 00:06:09.630
followed by thyroid
storm, which can happen,

00:06:09.630 --> 00:06:11.870
cause the thyroid, even in like,

00:06:11.870 --> 00:06:14.980
certain conditions like
Hashimoto's and Graves' disease.

00:06:14.980 --> 00:06:16.510
Sometimes it flips on and off

00:06:16.510 --> 00:06:18.260
between hyper and hypothyroid.

00:06:18.260 --> 00:06:20.210
It's not always so clearly defined,

00:06:20.210 --> 00:06:23.300
especially in the beginning
of the onset of disease

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:25.210
to later stages of disease.

00:06:25.210 --> 00:06:26.530
- Let's do a full STD panel

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:28.060
and check his genitals for chancres.

00:06:28.060 --> 00:06:29.610
- Well, first of all, you
should have checked him

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:31.710
for chancres beforehand
and you should have done

00:06:31.710 --> 00:06:33.970
a full STD panel before hand.

00:06:33.970 --> 00:06:36.260
It's like the cheapest test you can do.

00:06:36.260 --> 00:06:38.280
If you're talking about all these MRIs

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:40.360
that you're breaking,
costing millions of dollars,

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:42.840
the $300 STD panel would
have been worth it,

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:43.950
Don't you think?

00:06:43.950 --> 00:06:46.080
- You having any problems
with your vision?

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:49.098
- No, I have nystagmus. I've
had it since birth, I'm fine.

00:06:49.098 --> 00:06:51.300
- [Cameron] You're not fine,
you want a coma for two days.

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:52.490
There's something wrong with you.

00:06:52.490 --> 00:06:54.710
- Was something wrong
with me, now I'm better.

00:06:54.710 --> 00:06:56.400
Now I'd like to go home.

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:58.310
- The patient can always leave.

00:06:58.310 --> 00:07:01.387
Like, if he can think
about the consequences,

00:07:01.387 --> 00:07:04.550
if the patient can
verbalize those consequences

00:07:04.550 --> 00:07:06.600
and it's safe for them
to leave in that sense,

00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:07.630
they can choose to leave.

00:07:07.630 --> 00:07:10.770
They will leave against medical
advice, which is an AMA,

00:07:10.770 --> 00:07:12.900
but it's within their rights,
it's patient autonomy.

00:07:12.900 --> 00:07:14.450
- Wait, let us take you
all the way outside.

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:15.693
- I'm fine.

00:07:15.693 --> 00:07:18.340
- It doesn't matter, it's hospital rules.

00:07:18.340 --> 00:07:21.005
- Oh, screw the rules, I've
been on my back for four days.

00:07:21.005 --> 00:07:22.810
I need the exercise, right?

00:07:22.810 --> 00:07:24.730
- George, come on, let us
just take you to the taxi.

00:07:24.730 --> 00:07:26.450
- Don't worry, I may not be able

00:07:26.450 --> 00:07:28.564
to climb Everest, but I can walk.

00:07:28.564 --> 00:07:31.314
(suspense music)

00:07:35.001 --> 00:07:35.834
(dinging sound)
- First of all,

00:07:35.834 --> 00:07:38.230
if a patient has not gotten up

00:07:38.230 --> 00:07:40.070
since he's been admitted to the hospital,

00:07:40.070 --> 00:07:42.323
would get a PT evaluation to see

00:07:42.323 --> 00:07:44.470
if he's capable of walking on his own.

00:07:44.470 --> 00:07:47.150
And if he is not, he can
not safely go home alone.

00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:49.760
He would at least need to
go to a subacute rehab stay

00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:51.750
where he could learn
how to walk on his own

00:07:51.750 --> 00:07:52.670
and take care of himself.

00:07:52.670 --> 00:07:54.330
'Cause if a patient can't get up and walk,

00:07:54.330 --> 00:07:55.890
you're essentially setting
them up for failure

00:07:55.890 --> 00:07:57.065
by sending them home.

00:07:57.065 --> 00:07:58.037
- George?

00:07:58.037 --> 00:08:01.216
(glass smashes)

00:08:01.216 --> 00:08:03.027
- I think we should focus
on the coma and the fever.

00:08:03.027 --> 00:08:04.540
- We have a rather large piece

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:06.430
of tempered glass that begs to differ.

00:08:06.430 --> 00:08:08.960
- I just mean it's not connected.

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:10.280
- How could you possibly know?

00:08:10.280 --> 00:08:11.230
- Because I did it.

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:14.100
I didn't think he should be discharged,

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:16.918
so I gave him three grams of phenytoin.

00:08:16.918 --> 00:08:18.395
(spitting noise)

00:08:18.395 --> 00:08:19.860
- What hospital is this?

00:08:19.860 --> 00:08:22.500
She drugged the patient
so he wouldn't leave.

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:23.931
Oh my God.

00:08:23.931 --> 00:08:25.506
(clanking noise)

00:08:25.506 --> 00:08:26.339
(comical music playing)

00:08:26.339 --> 00:08:27.950
Don't poison your patients.

00:08:27.950 --> 00:08:29.360
Even if you think it's right for them

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:30.687
because you are not God.

00:08:30.687 --> 00:08:31.600
(screen whooshes)

00:08:31.600 --> 00:08:34.020
- [Sam] What would happen to her...?

00:08:34.020 --> 00:08:35.570
- Medical license loss?

00:08:35.570 --> 00:08:36.403
We'll do it in order.

00:08:36.403 --> 00:08:39.110
They find out, medical review committee,

00:08:39.110 --> 00:08:40.750
medical board suspension,

00:08:40.750 --> 00:08:42.790
followed by medical board reevaluation,

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:44.440
followed by loss of medical license,

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:46.030
either temporarily or forever,

00:08:46.030 --> 00:08:49.040
depending on how angry the patient is,

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:52.170
prior situations, et cetera, et cetera.

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:53.003
Lawyer up.

00:08:53.003 --> 00:08:55.190
- It can't be Chagas, he's
never been outside the country.

00:08:55.190 --> 00:08:56.330
- But his stomach has.

00:08:56.330 --> 00:08:58.930
The food we eat no longer
comes from America's heartland.

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:01.710
It comes from South America's
deforested jungle land

00:09:01.710 --> 00:09:04.350
where lettuce now grows and
lettuce pickers now poop.

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:05.640
Get a sample of his CSF.

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:06.690
- How are you going to get a sample

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:07.980
of his cerebral spinal fluid?

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:08.813
That's going to be tough.

00:09:08.813 --> 00:09:11.700
- [George] You want to
drill a hole in my head?

00:09:11.700 --> 00:09:14.709
It's gotta be something
other than a parasite.

00:09:14.709 --> 00:09:17.930
I buy my produce at the
best market in town,

00:09:17.930 --> 00:09:19.390
and I always wash it.

00:09:19.390 --> 00:09:21.190
- [Cameron] Leafy vegetables
can suck contaminated water

00:09:21.190 --> 00:09:22.710
through the roots right into the plant.

00:09:22.710 --> 00:09:25.600
- I've never heard this,
this sounds farfetched,

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:28.033
but I hope they researched this.

00:09:28.033 --> 00:09:30.783
(drilling noise)

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:34.520
Please tell me this is a
neurosurgeon doing this,

00:09:34.520 --> 00:09:35.733
Not like, Foreman.

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:39.210
It's Foreman, oh my God.

00:09:39.210 --> 00:09:41.100
These are they're all neurosurgeons,

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:44.540
infectious disease specialists,
family medicine doctors,

00:09:44.540 --> 00:09:47.570
cardiologists, they run MRI machines...

00:09:47.570 --> 00:09:49.430
Oh cramp!

00:09:49.430 --> 00:09:50.730
- What'd you do?

00:09:50.730 --> 00:09:52.003
- Nothing, why? What's wrong?

00:09:52.003 --> 00:09:54.080
- I can't, I can't see.

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:55.470
- Vision's blurry or you've lost it?

00:09:55.470 --> 00:09:57.460
- I didn't lose it, you took it from me.

00:09:57.460 --> 00:09:58.293
- [Cameron] George, calm down.

00:09:58.293 --> 00:09:59.300
- I can't see!

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:00.220
- This is actually why patients are

00:10:00.220 --> 00:10:02.170
kept awake during some neuro procedures,

00:10:02.170 --> 00:10:04.210
because in case you do touch something,

00:10:04.210 --> 00:10:05.360
you want to know right away

00:10:05.360 --> 00:10:07.440
so that you don't continue
doing damage to that area.

00:10:07.440 --> 00:10:09.241
- Blindness plus comma says diabetes.

00:10:09.241 --> 00:10:11.240
- No, blood sugar, urine dipstick,

00:10:11.240 --> 00:10:12.710
and hemoglobin A1-C are normal.

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:14.400
- Were normal, when you tested.

00:10:14.400 --> 00:10:15.480
He's been in and out of a coma,

00:10:15.480 --> 00:10:17.360
Whatever's going on is waxing and waning.

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:19.180
- That's not true because
the hemoglobin A1-C

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:20.790
gives you an average of the blood sugars

00:10:20.790 --> 00:10:21.970
over the last three months.

00:10:21.970 --> 00:10:23.680
So it doesn't mean it was normal today,

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:25.300
and it could be different tomorrow.

00:10:25.300 --> 00:10:27.570
It still will give you the
average of the last three months.

00:10:27.570 --> 00:10:28.783
So I don't agree with House here.

00:10:28.783 --> 00:10:30.910
- I'm not diabetic.

00:10:30.910 --> 00:10:32.150
- As soon as you drink
this, the sooner I get

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:34.580
to go waste my time with something else.

00:10:34.580 --> 00:10:35.590
- Get off of me.

00:10:35.590 --> 00:10:37.247
- No dessert till you
finished your dinner.

00:10:37.247 --> 00:10:39.510
(struggling sounds)

00:10:39.510 --> 00:10:40.660
- It's a classic House situation,

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:42.740
where he's just losing his
mind, fighting a patient.

00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:45.420
(shouting)

00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:46.253
- Go.

00:10:47.172 --> 00:10:49.150
- Oh wait, his liver is failing now?

00:10:49.150 --> 00:10:50.540
He's jaundiced? What's happening?

00:10:50.540 --> 00:10:52.090
- Get x-rays of his hands.

00:10:52.090 --> 00:10:54.671
Tell him the lung cancer is in
no way connected to obesity.

00:10:54.671 --> 00:10:57.080
- You don't think he'll
realize we're lying?

00:10:57.080 --> 00:10:58.793
- You're not, lung cancer
is got nothing to do with...

00:10:58.793 --> 00:11:01.360
- I meant about him having lung cancer.

00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:02.960
- You didn't notice his fingers?

00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:04.720
- I noticed they were fat.

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:06.420
- You should've pissed him off.

00:11:06.420 --> 00:11:08.610
He would have grabbed you and
you would have felt the bones.

00:11:08.610 --> 00:11:10.793
They're not just fat, they're clubbed.

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:15.830
- This is the first x-ray
they're getting? Are you joking?

00:11:15.830 --> 00:11:17.810
He was in a coma in the ICU

00:11:17.810 --> 00:11:19.873
and they're just getting an x-ray now?

00:11:21.340 --> 00:11:23.720
Oh, they're getting an x-ray of his hand.

00:11:23.720 --> 00:11:25.700
I thought there's the first
chest x-ray they're getting.

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:27.900
- Your tests were positive.

00:11:28.740 --> 00:11:31.998
You have a small cell lung carcinoma.

00:11:31.998 --> 00:11:34.540
It caused a paraneoplastic
neurologic syndrome.

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:36.450
- Paraneoplastic basically means that

00:11:36.450 --> 00:11:39.870
as a result of having this
tumor, it's secreted hormones

00:11:39.870 --> 00:11:43.270
that have altered the way
that his body behaves.

00:11:43.270 --> 00:11:45.180
- It's inoperable, but there there are

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:46.482
radiation treatments available.

00:11:46.482 --> 00:11:49.232
- (soft gasping)

00:11:50.300 --> 00:11:52.890
- They might give you a few more months.

00:11:52.890 --> 00:11:53.950
- I never smoked.

00:11:53.950 --> 00:11:56.500
- Not all lung cancer cases
are caused by smoking.

00:11:56.500 --> 00:11:58.043
Some are caused by asbestos.

00:11:58.043 --> 00:12:01.345
(footsteps walking away)

00:12:01.345 --> 00:12:04.520
(solemn music playing)

00:12:04.520 --> 00:12:06.710
I would ask if he had any
questions at that point.

00:12:06.710 --> 00:12:09.220
I mean, you're just delivering
a life-changing diagnosis,

00:12:09.220 --> 00:12:11.030
you spend 10 seconds and you leave.

00:12:11.030 --> 00:12:12.760
I think that's kind of cold.

00:12:12.760 --> 00:12:16.400
- Check out the harsh reality
of being 800 plus pounds here.

00:12:16.400 --> 00:12:19.489
Click it, check it out, as
always stay happy and healthy.

00:12:19.489 --> 00:12:22.572
(upbeat outro music)

